Phoenix Test Automation Framework
This repository houses the Phoenix Test Automation Framework, a robust, hybrid automation solution built using Java and Rest Assured. It is engineered for high-performance API testing, featuring advanced data handling, secure secret management, and comprehensive reporting.

🛠 Tech Stack & Key Libraries
The framework leverages a modern ecosystem to ensure scalability and ease of use:

Core Execution: Rest Assured for fluent API testing and validation.

Test Engine: TestNG for managing test execution, parallelization, and assertions.

Data Management:

OpenCSV & Apache POI: Robust handling of .csv and .xlsx data sources.

Poiji: Seamless mapping of Excel sheets to Java POJOs.

Java Faker: Generation of dynamic, realistic test data.

Database & Security:

MySQL & HikariCP: High-performance database connectivity and connection pooling.

Dotenv & Vault: Secure management of environment variables and sensitive credentials.

Optimization: Lombok to reduce boilerplate code in POJO and model classes.

Reporting & Logging:

Allure Reports: Rich, interactive test execution reports.

Log4j2: Asynchronous logging for detailed execution traces.

🏗 Framework Architecture
The framework is designed with a clear separation of concerns:

Utilities: Contains the CSV reader, Excel parser (Poiji), and database connectors.

POJOs: Data models representing API Request/Response bodies, simplified using Lombok.

Listeners: Integrated TestNG and Allure listeners for automated failure snapshots and reporting.

Constants: Centralized management of environment endpoints, database credentials, and browser configurations.

🚀 Getting Started
Prerequisites
Java 16 or higher.

Maven 3.6+.

Execution
To run the test suite via Maven, use the following command:

Bash
mvn clean test -DsuiteXmlFile=testng.xml
Generating Reports
The framework is pre-configured with the allure-maven plugin. After execution, generate and open the report using:

Bash
mvn allure:report
mvn allure:serve
📁 Project Structure
Plaintext
├── src/main/java
│   ├── api.endpoints      # API Route constants
│   ├── pojos              # Request/Response data models (Lombok)
│   ├── utils              # CSV, Excel (Poiji), DB (HikariCP), & Dotenv utils
│   └── report.config      # Allure & Log4j configurations
├── src/test/java
│   ├── tests              # API test scripts
│   └── base               # Base test setup and teardown
├── src/test/resources
│   ├── testdata           # CSV and Excel data files
│   └── .env               # Environment secrets (Git ignored)
└── pom.xml                # Project dependencies and plugins
🔒 Security & Environments
The framework utilizes .env files and HashiCorp Vault integration. Ensure your local .env file is populated with the necessary keys before execution to prevent authentication failures.
